[ti:Day 18]

[00:00.00]diverge [daɪˈvɜːdʒ]vi. (意见等)分歧；背离 例 There is a concern that euro zone economies may diverge when some regions are more affected than others by shocks. 搭 diverge from 与…相背离
[00:17.28]redeem [rɪˈdiːm]vt. 兑换；还清；补偿；挽回声誉；履行 (诺言等)；将(股票、债券等)兑成现金；赎回(抵押 品) 搭 redeem sth. from 赎回
[00:26.64]compatible [kəmˈpætəbl]a. 兼容的；相适合的；一致的；可 共存的，能相处的 例 This software is not compatible with your hardware. 搭 be compatible with 与…适合的；与…一致的
[00:40.92]computerise [kəmˈpjuːtəraɪz]vt. 用计算机处理；给…配备计 算机；使自动化 例 Their decision flve years ago to computerise the company is now paying dividends.
[00:55.20]incidental [ˌɪnsɪˈdentl]a. 偶然的；附带的 例 His success in career is not incidental at all.
[01:03.84]juxtapose [ˌdʒʌkstəˈpəʊz]vt. 并置，使并列(尤指为了比较 或对照) 例 Be sure to juxtapose your solutions so as to finish the task in the easiest and most efflcient way.
[01:18.96]aversion [əˈvɜːʃn]n. 厌恶，反感；讨厌的人 例 Risk aversion is one of the biggest factors driving allocation. 搭 aversion therapy 厌恶疗法 / have an aversion to... 对…反感
[01:34.32]retail [ˈriːteɪl]n. 零售，零卖 v. 零售
[01:37.56]lawsuit [ˈlɔːsuːt]n. 诉讼(尤指非刑事案件) 搭 bring a lawsuit against sb. 起诉某人
[01:44.52]expectancy [ɪkˈspektənsi]n. 期望；预期 例 All products have a life expectancy. 搭 expectancy theory 期望理论
[01:54.60]dock [dɒk]vt. 削减(薪金、供应、津贴等) n. 船坞；码 头 例 The dockers disburdened the merchandise at the dock and then left.
[02:05.28]trivial [ˈtrɪviəl]a. 琐碎的；轻微的；不重要的；平凡的 搭 put the trivial above the important 本末倒置 / trivial formalities 繁文缛节
[02:16.44]opaque [əʊˈpeɪk]a. 不透明的；不发光的；不传热的；不 清晰的；迟钝的 例 The institution has been opaque about its flnances over the years.
[02:28.08]sunset [ˈsʌnset]a. 夕阳西下的；衰落的
[02:31.20]upshot [ˈʌpʃɒt]n. 结果，结局；要点 例 The upshot of the talks is that both sides build up a partnership. 搭 in the upshot 最后，终于
[02:42.72]omnipotent [ɒmˈnɪpətənt]a. 全能的；有无限权力的
[02:46.92]undertake [ˌʌndəˈteɪk]vt. 承担，担任；从事；许诺，保证
[02:51.48]bounce [baʊns]vt. 使反弹；拒付并退回(支付) vi. (支票) 被银行退票 n. 未兑现支票；(股票价格的)反弹， 回升 例 The fact that her check bounced left her at a loss. 搭 bounce back 回升，复苏 / bounce sb. out of sth. 从某人处骗取财物
[03:09.00]working [ˈwɜːkɪŋ]a. 实用的；经营的，营运的
[03:12.48]notion [ˈnəʊʃn]n. 概念；想法，看法，打算；[pl.] 小件 日用品 搭 have a notion that 认为…派 notional a. 概念 上的(例：notional tax 概念税收)
[03:23.40]range [reɪndʒ]n. (产品的)种，类；一系列；幅度；变化 程度 搭 a range of 一系列
[03:29.04]engender [ɪnˈdʒendə(r)]v. (被)造成，(使)发生 例 Company love is possibly engendered due to a long-term work relationship. 搭 engender controversy 引起争议 / engender a wave 造成波动
[03:45.96]manual [ˈmænjuəl]n. 手册，指南；手工操作的器械 a. 用 手操作的，手工的；手册的
[03:51.48]bulky [ˈbʌlki]a. 大的；笨重的 例 These systems are usually bulky and difficult to use.
[03:59.52]start-up [ˈstɑːtʌp]n. 启动
[04:02.16]superiority [suːˌpɪəriˈɒrəti]n. 优越(性)；优势 例 The company has established absolute superiority over its opponents. 搭 sense of superiority 优越感
[04:16.68]toll [təʊl]n. 通行税；服务费；重大的代价 vt. 征收 vi. 征税 搭 levy toll on sb. 向某人征收税款 / take a toll 造成损失
[04:25.08]codetermination [kəʊdɪˌtɜːmɪˈneɪʃn]n. 共同决策制，劳资协同经营 制度；职工参与决策 例 The funds may, upon the codetermination of the owners, be used for maintaining such common parts as elevators and water tanks.
[04:44.76]hire [ˈhaɪə(r)]vt. 录用；雇用；租用 vi. 受雇；得到工 作 n. 租金；酬金；被雇用的人 例 It's obvious that an employer cannot afford to hire incapable workers. 搭 hire out 出租
[04:59.04]underpaid [ˌʌndəˈpeɪd]a. 所得报酬过低的 例 The hard-working salesman never complained of being underpaid.
[05:09.36]espionage [ˈespiənɑːʒ]n. 刺探，谍报活动 例 Only the big boss knows the detailed plan to protect against espionage.
[05:20.28]duration [djuˈreɪʃn]n. 持续，持续期间
[05:23.64]denounce [dɪˈnaʊns]vt. 谴责，指责；告发 例 Many web users strongly denounce some e-commerce sites for selling diluted cosmetics. 搭 denounce...for... 因…谴责… / denounce sb. to 向…告发某人
[05:41.28]well-being [ˈwelbiːɪŋ]n. 利益；福利；健康 例 A positive corporate culture can contribute to both the company's development and the well-being of the employees. 搭 psychological well-being 心理健康
[06:00.24]membership [ˈmembəʃɪp]n. 成员资格；会员身份；全体会 员；成员数
[06:05.16]trader [ˈtreɪdə(r)]n. 商人；商船；证券投资人
[06:08.88]zeal [ziːl]n. 热心，热情；热忱 例 To finish the project on time, they plunged into their work with a determined zeal.
[06:19.68]breach [briːtʃ]v. 突破；违反；不履行 n. 违背 例 The snooty envoy seems to regard meeting anyone below the prime minister as a breach of protocol.
[06:33.00]consolidate [kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt]v. (使)联合；(使)巩固；(使) 加强 例 The three colleges will consolidate and form a bigger university next year. 搭 consolidate one's position 巩固地位
[06:49.56]competency [ˈkɒmpɪtənsi]n. 资格；能力 例 In order to establish the supply inventory, resources must be classified by both competency and skill. Not all freelance positions are home- based. 搭 competency in doing sth. 做…的能力
[07:11.52]inflow [ˈɪnfləʊ]n. 流入(物) 例 Extra capital inflow for the start-up company will be forthcoming as planned.
[07:22.20]decertify [ˌdiːˈsɜːtɪfaɪ]v. 收回(或取消)证件 例 Under the current rules, if the authority wants to decertify a lab, it must revoke the accreditation of the entire institution.
[07:39.36]embroil [ɪmˈbrɔɪl]vt. 使卷入；使混乱 例 Do your best to avoid our products being embroiled in any dispute. 搭 embroil sb. in 使某人卷入纠纷
[07:51.72]windfall [ˈwɪndfɔːl]n. 横财；意外的收获
[07:55.20]nationalise [ˈnæʃnəlaɪz]vt. 使国有化
[07:58.80]shakeout [ˈʃeɪkaʊt]n. 轻度经济衰退；股票市场震动；(公 司、产品等)被淘汰 例 A shakeout in America's economy is unavoidable.
[08:09.24]disposition [ˌdɪspəˈzɪʃn]n. 部署；处置；支配 搭 defensive disposition 防御部署
[08:16.32]zoom [zuːm]n. 急速上升；缩放；变焦摄影 vi. 突然扩 大；急速上升 vt. 使摄像机移动 例 House prices suddenly zoomed at the beginning of this year.
[08:27.84]span [spæn]vt. 跨越；横跨；持续 n. 全长；跨度；幅 度 例 It takes about fifteen minutes to span the river. 搭 spick and span 崭新的，极干净的 / time span 时间跨度
[08:40.68]coup [kuː]n. 突然的一击；突然行动；成功之举；好主 意 例 Getting the contract was quite a coup. 搭 make a great coup 大获成功
[08:50.52]indignant [ɪnˈdɪɡnənt]a. 愤怒的；愤慨的 例 He was very indignant with his boss's unjust treatment. 搭 be indignant at sth. 为某事感到愤慨 / be indignant with sb. 对某人感到愤怒
[09:06.00]perennial [pəˈreniəl]a. 长期的，持久的；一再的 例 The cosmetics of this brand are a perennial favourite.
[09:15.60]unravel [ʌnˈrævl]vt. 解开，拆散；阐明；解决 例 The investors' focus remains on whether the government will unravel the fiscal cliff problem.
[09:28.92]prototype [ˈprəʊtətaɪp]n. 原型；样品
[09:32.40]chart [tʃɑːt]vt. 绘制图表；详细计划 vi. 排入最畅销品 n. 图表 例 They tried to chart the sea area between Norway and Denmark. 搭 off the charts 水平极高
[09:45.00]qualified [ˈkwɒlɪfaɪd]a. 有资格的；合格的；受限制的；有 保留的
